WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:04.830
Where can a bank keep lending
in a recession, and what risk remains?

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:08.610
I kept the credit policy fixed
across both scenarios.

00:00:09.145 --> 00:00:12.925
In the console, I selected EC2 Windows,

00:00:13.095 --> 00:00:17.325
set the cohort to 750
synthetic applicants,

00:00:17.435 --> 00:00:20.555
and chose Amazon S3 for the results.

00:00:21.072 --> 00:00:22.862
I submitted the campaign once.

00:00:22.902 --> 00:00:26.882
The console refreshed progress
every 30 seconds

00:00:26.922 --> 00:00:30.672
as each application went through
Baseline and Recession Energy.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:35.020
On AWS, about 45 minutes of computation

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.680
produced 1,500 decisions

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.780
and 16,320 daily monitoring records.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:48.880
In Baseline, 318 businesses were funded
or referred for review.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.080
Under stress, that fell to 72.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:55.670
Tableau shows how many
actually received financing.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:59.840
110 in Baseline, 26 under stress.

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:05.200
In Baseline, the lender advanced
$1.57 million.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:09.690
Under stress, that fell to about $491,000.

00:01:10.125 --> 00:01:13.465
Twenty-three businesses got
their full request either way.

00:01:14.025 --> 00:01:18.945
Merchant 000225 received
$150,000 for inventory,

00:01:19.355 --> 00:01:23.815
with 8.68% of eligible sales
going toward repayment.

00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:30.193
By day 120, this business still owed
about $20,000 in Baseline.

00:01:30.643 --> 00:01:36.573
Under stress, it owed about $1,350 more
on the same advance.

00:01:37.072 --> 00:01:39.722
The stress account went
into servicing review.

00:01:40.182 --> 00:01:42.682
Its booked terms stayed in force.

00:01:43.217 --> 00:01:45.167
Twenty-five accounts paid off.

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:48.437
One merchant carried
all the remaining exposure.

00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:50.597
That concentration matters

00:01:50.637 --> 00:01:54.357
when deciding where to extend credit
as conditions change.

